## roles :- an ansible roles is a way to organize and reuse your ansible code.
            instead of putting everything in one large playbook we divide the automation in seprate groups/folders.

## why do we use roles? ##
> suppose we want to install and Configure nginx
  without a roles :
  
    - name: Install Nginx
      hosts: all
      become: true

      tasks:
        - name: Install nginx
          apt:
            name: nginx
            state: present

        - name: Start nginx
          service:
            name: nginx
            state: started

     as your project become bigger ,the playbook become difficult to manage .

    with role:

    nginx/
    ├── tasks/
    ├── handlers/
    ├── templates/
    ├── files/
    ├── vars/
    ├── defaults/
    └── meta/  
   now each part has specific purpose.

