## ansible handlers ##

 an ansible handler is a special task that runs only when another taks changes something .
 most commonly handler is used to restart or reload services after configuration changes.

 suppose you modify the nginx configuration: 

    - name: Configure Nginx
      hosts: all
      become: true

      tasks:
        - name: Copy nginx configuration
          copy:
            src: nginx.conf
            dest: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
          notify:
            - Restart Nginx

      handlers:
        - name: Restart Nginx
          service:
            name: nginx
            state: restarted


  ## how it works ##

    Task changes file
          ↓
    notify: Restart Nginx
          ↓
    Handler runs
          ↓
    Nginx restarts      

note :- if the copy task dosen't change anything, the handler will not run.

